# Lens Flare on D3D11 (0) or in the render graph's tonemap chain (1): Whiterun at 13:00 in clear weather, then
# Dragonsreach, a shot of each. Compare the two runs' shots.
# The chain runs on the graph only when every enabled sub-effect is ported. Lens Flare turns Composite on, so Composite's
# ORG port must be merged too. The main session sets in SettingsUser.json, under "PostProcessing":
#   "Lens Flare": { "enabled": true }   (Composite follows it)
#   every other sub-effect without an ORG port: { "enabled": false }
#   "Lens Flare": { "settings": { "GhostModeInt": 1 } }   Quality (FFT, the default). 0 = Fast (procedural ghosts and
#   Kawase blur), 2 = Ultra (per-ghost kernel scales: also give some "Ghosts" different "KernelScale" values, e.g. 0.5 and 2.0,
#   for several kernel groups). Raise "Intensity" to 1.0 and lower "ThresholdEV" to 0 to make the flare easy to see.
# Effects11 must not own the tonemap. With CS_ORG_POST_PROCESSING=1 the log shows
#   "[ORG] Post Processing: chain built (input, lens-flare, composite, ...)" and "the chain runs on the render graph",
# or "the chain runs on D3D11: ..." naming what keeps it there.
CS_ORG_POST_PROCESSING=0
DXVK_DEBUG=hang
VK_LOADER_LAYERS_DISABLE=*nsight*
CS_DCLF_TEST_COMMANDS=600:set timescale to 0;601:set gamehour to 13;602:fw 81a;700:coc Whiterun;2000:fw 81a;2400:dclf:shot=whiterun;2500:coc WhiterunDragonsreach;3600:dclf:shot=dragonsreach
CS_DCLF_TEST_EXIT=3700
CS_PP_ONLY=Lens Flare,Composite
